      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand about hip-width with the bar on the floor close to the shins and grip it overhand slightly wider than shoulder width.",
        "movement": "Keep the bar close as the hips and knees extend, then rapidly extend the hips, knees, and ankles and shrug before bending the elbows to pull under.",
        "endpoint": "Receive the bar across the clavicles and front shoulders in a quarter squat with the elbows pointing forward.",
        "returnPhase": "Stand fully from the catch, then lower the bar under control to the floor before the next repetition.",
        "controlledJoints": "Complete the lower-body extension before bending the elbows and control hip, knee, and ankle flexion in the catch.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Keep the bar close, brace the trunk, and maintain a secure two-hand grip.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Starting from the hang changes the exercise into a hang clean.", "Receiving below a power quarter squat changes the exercise into a full clean.", "Failing to stand from the catch leaves the repetition incomplete."]
